From de536bd8b1009b6c38888db6502925620f65d7d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:40:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] ##arch: Emulate the USSE forms of the fourth probe
 round

A fourth round of client fills on an SGX545, now with a different input
per pixel, pinned the test channels, rlp, the video differences, the
dual issue and the repeats of the colour groups, and the ESIL follows:

- test channels: one result per channel, the 32-bit result as channel
  0, a 16-bit op's halves as channels 0 and 2; a channel without a lane
  tests as a positive non-zero value; andall/orall over all four,
  and02/or02 over channels 0 and 2
- rlp d, s, pN: d = s << 1 | pN, then pN = bit 31 of s; predicate
  numbers 4 and up alias p0-p3
- adif: |a - b| per byte; adifsum: their sum plus a 16-bit half of s0
- unpcku16c10/unpcks16c10: no conversion, three bits of lane 0 into the
  low half whatever the selects
- sop2, fpma and the integer dot products with .repeatN: every operand
  advances per iteration
- dual issue for the pairs that co-issue cleanly: both operations read
  before either writes, the secondary wins a shared destination,
  .repeat2 runs both, the predicate covers both

Not modelled: fdsx/fdsy and efo.gpiext (they read other pixels of the
2x2 quad), i3 (the next pixel's i0), smp, the dual-issue pairs that
share a unit, ima32 as a secondary and the c10 colour operands.

14 new and 2 changed test/db/esil/usse tests. The microkernel uses none
of these forms: 84.2% of its words still have ESIL; 662 of 153466
decodable random words do (was 527).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
